# Draft. Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# GitHub reads CODEOWNERS in `.github/`, in the root, or in `docs/` (first one found, in that order).
# A file in `.github/` can have its own owner line, as the docs advise (see the last lines).
# The last matching line wins. The owner of a path gets a review request for each pull request that changes the path.
# The owner is @mmccalla (decision of Mark, 2026-11-03).
# The ruleset in `repo-settings/plan.md` sets "require code owner review" to false.
# With one owner, a code owner review would lock the owner out of his own pull requests.

# Default owner for the whole repository
